{
  "task": "binary-multiplication",
  "experiment": "corrected-dataset-fix (BMF1: dataset construction + audit)",
  "description": "Corrected binary-multiplication dataset preserving Butoi et al.'s mixed negative-generation strategy (50% uniform-random / 50% hard-negative half). Hard negatives are constructed via a single-bit flip in u_z (LSB-first, excluding bit 0/the LSB) of a genuine positive -- structurally guaranteed to preserve all five shortcut features (operator_count_is_one, equals_count_is_one_after_operator, fields_well_formed, length_sufficient, lsb_consistent), while making the claimed product genuinely wrong. Bit-flip position swept across low/mid/high tertiles with the target held fixed across retries (Option A discipline). Reuses the exact target_computation_pairs construction validated in the Phase 3 causal-patching pilot (analysis/phase3_binmult_counterfactual_design.py), extended to full-dataset scale.",
  "random_seed": 20260722,
  "language_output_directory": "languages/binary-multiplication-fixed",
  "splits_generated": {
    "train": {
      "n": 10000,
      "length_range": [
        0,
        40
      ]
    },
    "validation-short": {
      "n": 1000,
      "length_range": [
        0,
        40
      ]
    },
    "test": {
      "n": 5010,
      "length_range": [
        0,
        500
      ]
    }
  },
  "known_simplifications_vs_original_pipeline": [
    "No cross-split deduplication of positive examples.",
    "Hard-negative construction rejects (resamples entirely) when n_z < 2 or the target tertile has no candidate bit position (bit 0 always excluded) for that sample -- minor documented distributional deviations for the hard-negative half only.",
    "No log-probabilities.txt: BinaryArithmeticOperation.supports_log_probability() is False.",
    "The magnitude-scaling confound (LSB-first encoding means 'high'-tertile bit flips change the claimed value by an astronomically larger amount than 'low'-tertile flips) is inherent to the task's own encoding and is NOT corrected by this construction -- reported (magnitude_change_distribution_by_tertile) for downstream training-time analysis, matching the same documented, uncorrected confound in binary-addition/compute-sqrt."
  ],
